.TH XD\-SERVICES 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-services \- the Services console for systemd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-services
.OP \-\-user
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-services
is Windows XP's Services console with systemd's services in it: those of
the system manager and of the user's own manager, on the System and User
tabs.
Services can be started, stopped and restarted, and their startup type
changed.
.PP
Changing system services goes through polkit, so
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for a password; the user's own services don't need one.
systemd has no paused state, so Pause and Resume are greyed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-user
Open on the User tab.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR xd\-admintools (1)
